<title>JAPAN: Saudi Aramco cuts April propane, butane prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts April propane, butane prices.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's state-owned oil firm Saudi Aramco said on Monday it had cut its propane contract price for April by $72 from the previous month to $198 per tonne, and its price for butane by $70 to $207 per tonne.  </p>
<p>The propane price for April is $6 per tonne higher than the same month a year ago, while the price of butane is $19 higher than last year.</p>
<p>The Saudi contract price is loosely based on the results of three monthly spot tenders and the company's own assessment of spot market trends. -- Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-3432-8837</p>
</text>
